Q41) How to explain this in interviews in one minute?
A)
- "I built a modular ASP.NET Core 9 solution where Core contains all domain contracts and entities, Infrastructure provides swappable implementations for data access (EF Core + SQLite), queuing (in-memory Channel or Azure Service Bus), and caching (in-memory or Redis). The API layer uses controller-based endpoints with API versioning, ProblemDetails error standardization, correlation ID middleware, and health checks. A BackgroundService worker dequeues analysis jobs and processes them via a mock orchestrator that generates CVE risk analysis without any external AI dependency. The Web layer is an MVC frontend that proxies to the API and renders results in a tabbed Bootstrap 5 dashboard. The design is Clean-Architecture-aligned with 25 passing tests covering unit, integration, and end-to-end workflow scenarios."

